            text: "Alligator cracking is fatigue failure. The asphalt flexes under load more than it can tolerate, either because the base beneath it has softened or washed out, or because the asphalt itself has aged and gone brittle. The interconnected pattern is the surface breaking up because it is no longer properly supported.",
