            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Follow the patch manufacturer's cure time, which is usually 24 to 48 hours for trowel-grade patch in warm dry weather and considerably longer in cool or humid conditions. Cold patch asphalt should be driven on for a few weeks to compact and shed its solvents before it is sealed. Sealing too early traps solvent and the sealer stays soft.",
